# Accumulate Follow-up Tweaks

When a user asks for a small follow-up tweak on the same just-delivered change
and indicates they are not satisfied yet:

- Prefer undoing the last assistant commit and accumulating the tweak(s) in the
  same change set.
- Use `git reset --soft HEAD~1` only when the last commit is the assistant's
  recent commit for that topic and it is safe to fold.
- Re-commit once the user accepts the result, so the history keeps one clean
  commit per accepted change.

Safety checks before undoing a commit:

- Do not drop user-authored work.
- If there are unrelated staged/unstaged changes or the history is ambiguous,
  ask the user before rewriting local commits.
- Never push rewritten history unless the user explicitly asks to push.
